+/*
+ * Formats mesa3d cannot allocate/import directly (NV12, NV21, YVU420, YVU420_ANDROID, BGR888,
+ * see get_gbm_format()) and 1D R8 (BLOB) buffers are "spoofed": minigbm computes the plane
+ * strides/offsets itself (drv_bo_from_format) and the whole buffer is backed by ONE linear R8
+ * 2D texture of SPOOFED_BO_WIDTH bytes per row. mesa3d only ever sees that R8 texture; mapping
+ * it at (0, 0) yields a flat view of the buffer to which the minigbm plane offsets are applied.
+ * Allocation (gbm_mesa_bo_create), import (gbm_mesa_bo_import) and map (gbm_mesa_bo_map) MUST
+ * all describe the same geometry, so it is computed in one place.
